Tee Command:
It will be used to print and store the output at the same time. > or >> only store the output to file. But tee command will print the output on cli and store the output to file.
ls -ltr | tee filename or ls -ltr | tee testfile .
This command will store and print the output to file and cli. This is same as > redirect
If we want to append the output to file using tee command need to use below command
ls -ltr | tee -a filename
We can able to store output to multiple files at same time using tee command
ls -ltr | tee -a file1 file2 file3
